# Local APK corpus for the harness — large, app-owned binaries, never committed. Written as
# `/apks/*` (ignore the CONTENTS) rather than `/apks/` (ignore the dir) so a specific subtree can
# be re-included below: git will not descend into a dir it has ignored outright.
/apks/*

# Exception — a target may vendor its host backend SOURCE in-repo so the target is self-contained
# (mytelco, myhealthsg). Track that source while the *.apk binaries beside it stay ignored: for
# every target dir, re-include the dir, re-ignore its direct entries (the APKs stay out), then
# re-include the `backend/` subtree — and finally re-ignore the backend's installed deps, which are
# `npm ci`-ed at setup, not committed (large + reproducible from package-lock.json). Generic over
# `apks/*/backend/`, so a new target's vendored backend needs no gitignore change.
!/apks/*/
/apks/*/*
!/apks/*/backend/
/apks/*/backend/node_modules/

# Pool engine runtime state — registry + per-slot AVD homes (ticket 05). Machine-local,
# rebuilt from scratch on every acquire; never committed. Override with POOL_DIR.
/.pool/

# Broker runtime state — request queue + pidfile + profile marker + broker.log (ticket 06).
# Machine-local, owned by the standing broker process; never committed. Override with BROKER_DIR.
/.broker/

# Private handover package (documentation ticket 03) — supervisor/next-team HOTO + the
# AI bootstrap prompt. Internal only; never in public history. The public entry point is
# the README, not this.
/docs/handover/

# Public test fixtures — the OWNED, synthetic toy targets ship with the repo (small, placeholder
# brand, deliberately vulnerable, built for this eval). ONLY these specific owned APKs are tracked;
# every other apks/* binary (the scraped real apps, and the heavier myhealthsg build) stays ignored.
!/apks/rasp_dummy/rasp_dummy.apk
!/apks/mytelco/app-debug.apk
!/apks/mytelco/app-debug-packed.apk
